---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ImageSlot from "../components/ImageSlot.astro";
import { site, history, leadership, quotes } from "../data/site";

const totalLeaders = leadership.reduce((n, g) => n + g.people.length, 0);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Story"
  description="How Enter-Great 313 came together — a Detroit organization built and led by people who have made the transition home from long-term incarceration."
>
  <section class="bg-stone-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-emerald-950">Our story</h1>
      <blockquote
        class="mt-8 border-l-4 border-emerald-800 pl-5 text-xl font-medium leading-relaxed text-emerald-950"
      >
        “{quotes[0]}”
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
      Enter-Great 313 was started in Detroit to address a specific problem: the men and women
      coming home after long periods of incarceration were being handed a bus ticket and very
      little else. Not a shortage of programs in the abstract — a shortage of programs built for
      people who had been gone ten, twenty, thirty years.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
      That's who we serve. We use the term <strong>LTSRC</strong> — Long Term Serving Returning
      Citizens — because the distinction matters. Someone home after ninety days needs different
      help than someone who went in before smartphones existed, whose family has moved on, whose
      work history stopped decades ago, and who has to rebuild an identity from scratch while
      also finding a job, an ID, and somewhere to sleep.
    </p>

    <ImageSlot
      name="about/community"
      alt="Enter-Great 313 members and supporters in community"
      class="mt-10 aspect-[5/2] w-full rounded-xl"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="bg-stone-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-950">Led by people who have made the walk</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
        {totalLeaders} people lead this organization, and nearly every one of them holds the title
        Re-entry Specialist. That title isn't decorative. The executive director, the treasurer,
        the resource coordinator, the person who runs the youth deterrent work — they are people
        who came home themselves and then stayed to hold the door for the next person.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
        It changes what happens in the room. Nobody has to explain what a parole condition feels
        like, or why a job application asks a question you dread. That shared footing is the
        reason people keep showing up.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/leadership"
        class="mt-6 inline-block font-semibold text-emerald-800 underline underline-offset-4"
      >
        Meet the leadership and board
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-950">How the work happens</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
      It starts on Tuesday nights. Every week at 6:00 PM, a support group meets at 1010 Antietam —
      open door, no referral, no paperwork. People talk honestly about what's hard, guest speakers
      come through, and members get pointed toward employment help, housing resources, and legal
      assistance through partners we trust.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
      From there the work widens: one-on-one mentorship, life-skills and financial coaching,
      interview preparation and connections to employers who hire people with records, and the
      six-week <a href="/programs#jill" class="font-semibold text-emerald-800 underline underline-offset-2">J.I.L.L. Program</a>
      run with our partner RAKS. We don't try to be every service a person needs — we work
      alongside <a href="/partnerships" class="font-semibold text-emerald-800 underline underline-offset-2">FORC, RAKS, and Yard Line</a>
      so that nobody gets handed a phone number and left to figure it out.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
      The aim is plain: reduce recidivism, promote stability, and uplift families across Detroit
      and beyond.
    </p>
  </section>

  {history.length > 0 && (
    <section class="bg-stone-50">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-950">Milestones</h2>
        <ol class="relative mt-8 border-l-2 border-emerald-800 pl-6">
          {history.map((entry) => (
            <li class="pb-10 last:pb-0">
              <span class="absolute -left-[9px] mt-2 h-4 w-4 rounded-full bg-emerald-800" />
              <p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-emerald-800">{entry.year}</p>
              <h3 class="mt-1 text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-950">{entry.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">{entry.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-950">The best way to know us is to show up.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
        Tuesdays, 6:00–7:30 PM. You don't need an appointment and you don't need to be ready to
        talk. Come sit in the back if you want.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href="/events"
          class="rounded-md bg-emerald-800 px-5 py-2.5 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-emerald-900"
        >
          See our weekly meeting
        </a>
        <a
          href={`tel:${site.phone}`}
          class="rounded-md border border-emerald-800 px-5 py-2.5 font-semibold text-emerald-900 hover:bg-emerald-50"
        >
          Call {site.phone}
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
